| `commit subject hook` | The local `commit-subject` hook runs `scripts/commit_subject.py --message-file` at `commit-msg` and refuses a subject outside the declared policy. | `pre-commit install` installs both hook types through `default_install_hook_types`. | [`commit_subject.types`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`commit_subject.scope_chars`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Installation is manual. A `MERGE_HEAD` beside the message exempts a merge. The hook also exempts `fixup! `, `squash! ` and `amend! ` subjects; the history gate still judges them unsquashed. Revert subjects receive no exemption. Not for committed history: the subject history gate judges it. | [Deterministic checks](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
